&lt;p&gt;The Senior Data Protection Manager supports the Data Protection Officer and the Data Protection Team in performing the following tasks, under the supervision of the Data Protection Officer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Your Role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and update at least on annual basis and/or whenever necessary (eg. material changes in laws or in the company organization) relevant data protection policies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and update the personal data processing inventories (ie. Records of Processing Activities according to art. 30 GDPR).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safeguard the rights of data subjects, e.g., by checking notifications and reporting obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train employees, with regard to data protection and data privacy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support in the selection, contract design, monitoring of contractors who perform data processing on behalf of the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the regularity of data processing, perform prior checks or support the data protection impact assessments with relevant departments for processing involving sensitive data or falling into medium/high risks for the data subjects (including, but not limited to risks connected to cross-border data transfers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on relevant and data protection-relevant legal provisions, on data protection-relevant contracts and internal company guidelines, and on all individual data protection issue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft the annual activity report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft ad-hoc reports for the management and/or the department, if deemed required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform control and monitoring activities to ensure compliance with data protection regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct investigation on (potential) data breaches and ensuring reporting to Data Protection Authorities and/or affected data subjects and Cooperation Partners is performed when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assume the role of Deputy DPO if required by the bank.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;We&#39;d love to see&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
